      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Meaning is found in the absolute honesty of the cessation, not in the struggle against it. If he truly lets go, it's not giving up; it's finally ceasing the performance that has been draining him. That final, quiet acceptance is the most potent truth you can give him. It validates the exhaustion, making the silence the only honest word left in the narrative.",
